      <div type="clause" n="17">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 17</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="17" corresp="#wit-e"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Af_17.lnote.oe.13"/><pb n="58" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif hwa oðrum his unmagan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Af_17.lnote.oe.21"/> oðfæste, ⁊ he hine on ðære<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#Af_17.lnote.oe.22"/> fæstinge forferie, getriowe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#Af_17.lnote.oe.23"/> hine facnes se<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#Af_17.lnote.oe.24"/> ðe hine fede, gif hine<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#Af_17.lnote.oe.25"/> hwa hwelces<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="26" target="#Af_17.lnote.oe.26"/> teo.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="17" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="58" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif hwa oðrum his unmagan oðfæste, ⁊ he<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_17.lnote.oe.5"/> hine on þære fæstinge forferie, getreowsie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_17.lnote.oe.8"/> hine facnes se ðe hine fede, gif hine hwa hwylces teo.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_17.lnote.oe.7"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="17" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="58" ed="#liebermann"/>Be oðru<hi rend="italic">m</hi> his unmagu<hi rend="italic">m<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_17.lnote.oe.3"/></hi> ætfæsteð. Gyf hwá oðru<hi rend="italic">m</hi> his unmagan oðfæste, ⁊ he hine on ðære fæstinge forferie, getreowige<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_17.lnote.oe.4"/> hine facnes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_17.lnote.oe.5-2"/> se ðe hine fede, gyf hwá hine hwylces téo.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="17" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="59" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis alii suum quid<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Af_17.lnote.oe.15"/> imbecille commendet<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Af_17.lnote.oe.16"/>, et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Af_17.lnote.oe.17"/> in illa commendatione moriatur, adlegiet se facinoris qui pascebat illud, si ab aliquo compellatur inde.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Af_17.lnote.oe.18"/></ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="72" ed="#attenborough"/>[Ðe oðrum his unmagum ætfæsteð.] Gif hwa oðrum his unmagan oðfæste, ⁊ he hine on ðære fæstinge forferie, getriowe<ptr type="editorNote" n="7" target="#Af_17.attnote.fn.7"/> hine facnes se ðe hine fede, gif hine hwa hwelces teo.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="19" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="310" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Gif hwa oðrum his unmagan oðfæste, ⁊ he hine on ðære fæstinge forferie, getriowe hine facnes se ðe hine fede, gif hine hwa hwelces teo.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="59" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn einer einem anderen seinen Unmündigen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_17.lnote.de.1"/> anvertraut, und dieser in der Pflegehut<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_17.lnote.de.2"/> stirbt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_17.lnote.de.3"/>, so schwöre sich<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_17.lnote.de.4"/> der, welcher diesen verpflegt, von der Verschuldung rein, falls ihn jemand irgend welcher bezichtigt.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If someone entrusts his minor child to another, and the child dies in that fostering, let the one who fed him clear himself by oath of wrongdoing, if anyone accuses him of any.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="73" ed="#attenborough"/>If anyone entrusts a [child or other] helpless person<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Af_17.attnote.n.1"/> who is dependent on him to another, and the person accepting the charge causes the death of the person committed to him, he who nurtured him shall clear himself of criminal intention, if anyone prefers such an accusation against him.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="412" ed="#whitelock"/>If anyone entrusts to another one of his helpless dependants, and he dies<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#Af_17.whinote.n.2"/> during that time of fostering, he who reared him is to clear himself of guilt, if anyone accuses him of any.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="311" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If someone entrusts his dependent [child] to another, and [the guardian] allows it to die while in that care, let [the guardian] who supported him clear himself of wrongdoing, if someone accuses him of something.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="282"><label>possibly derived from</label> <ref target="clause:Af_El-to-35">Af El 35–36</ref> <quote>Af 17 (if not Af Int. 35 – 36)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="311"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Af_El-to-28">Af El 28</ref> <quote>MP §28 discusses the responsibility of a person who has had any property entrusted to him; he must likewise swear his innocence</quote></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_17.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Capiteltrennung nach B’s Rubricator Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">chapter division in Ld following B’s rubricator</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_17.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">unmaga <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> -gum <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">unmaga So; -gum Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_17.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðere <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðere Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_17.lnote.oe.23" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">getrywige <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">getrywige Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_17.lnote.oe.24" n="24" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">facnesse ðe <hi rend="italic">E So;</hi> facnysse se ðe <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">facnesse ðe E So; facnysse se ðe Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_17.lnote.oe.25" n="25" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_17.lnote.oe.26" n="26" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hwelce <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> hwylces <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hwelce So; hwylces Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_17.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written above</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_17.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sie <hi rend="italic">übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sie written above</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_17.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">e <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">e on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_17.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">59</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_17.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">59</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">emendet <hi rend="italic">Brti</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">emendet Brti</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_17.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">59</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">et <hi rend="italic">und Rest des Capitels fehlt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">et and the rest of the chapter lacking in K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_17.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">59</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">folgt c.</hi> 20 <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">c. 20 follows in Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_17.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">unmagan <hi rend="italic">bessern Edd.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">edd. correct to unmagan</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_17.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">neu</hi> s <hi rend="italic">vor</hi> ige</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">s before ige added by a later hand</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_17.lnote.oe.5-2" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">neu geänd. in</hi> facnesse se</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered by a later hand to facnesse se</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_17.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">55</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Wer anderem seinen Unmündigen anvertraut’ Rb B</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘Whoever entrusts his ward to another’ Rb B</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_17.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">55</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Erziehung 4; Gefährdeeid 1; <hi rend="italic">Wb: unmaga</hi> über Inst’s Fehler. Phillipps (<hi rend="italic">Agsä. R.</hi> 153), Price-Thorpe, Schmid (‘wahrscheinlich’ 671), Toller <hi rend="italic">Dict.</hi> s. v. <hi rend="italic">fæsting</hi> verstehen ‘Kind’. Der frühere Irrtum ‘Vieh’ entstand wohl aus Q’s Zufügung <hi rend="italic">quid,</hi> die in I. Rez. besser fehlt. Die enge Bed. ‘Kind’ ist aber nicht die alleinige bei Grimm <hi rend="italic">DRA</hi> 412 oder Kolderup-Rosenvinge <hi rend="italic">Antiqua Canuti versio</hi> 83, der auch eine durch Mangel an Körper- oder Geisteskraft unmündige Person gemeint sein lässt</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Erziehung 4; Gefährdeeid 1; <hi rend="italic">Wb: unmaga</hi> on the error of the Inst. Phillipps (<hi rend="italic">Agsä. R.</hi> 153), Price-Thorpe, Schmid (‘probably’ 671), Toller <hi rend="italic">Dict.</hi> s. v. <hi rend="italic">fæsting</hi> understand ‘child’. The earlier error ‘cattle’ probably arose from Q’s addition <hi rend="italic">quid,</hi> which is better absent in rec. I. The narrow meaning ‘child’ is not, however, the only one in Grimm <hi rend="italic">DRA</hi> 412 or in Kolderup-Rosenvinge <hi rend="italic">Antiqua Canuti versio</hi> 83, who lets the word also denote a person lacking legal capacity through want of bodily or mental strength</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_17.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">55</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘ihm’ Schmid falsch. <hi rend="italic">Vgl.</hi> zum reflexiven Gebrauche: <hi rend="italic">þe aferige</hi> ‘dich entfernest’ bei Toller; ‘sterben’ Wülfing <hi rend="italic">Syntax</hi> II 13</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘to him’ Schmid, wrongly. On the reflexive use <hi rend="italic">cf.</hi> <hi rend="italic">þe aferige</hi> ‘removest thyself’ in Toller; ‘die’ Wülfing <hi rend="italic">Syntax</hi> II 13</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_17.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">55</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">s. Wb: getreowian</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">see Wb: getreowian</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_17.attnote.fn.7" n="7" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">72</biblScope></bibl><label>getriowe</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">getreowige</hi>. B. <hi rend="italic">getreowsie</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Af_17.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">195</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Primarily, no doubt, children are referred to.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Af_17.whinote.n.2" n="2" source="#whitelock"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">412</biblScope></bibl><label>dies</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">So Liebermann, but the dictionaries and Attenborough take the expression <hi rend="italic">hine forferie,</hi> which seems unique, to mean “cause or allow to die”, and the subject would then be the guardian.</seg></note>
